/* v97: art the Prowl page shows, served from the worker so it costs the Shopify page nothing (Shopify caps the page
   body at 512 KB). GET /art/<name> answers it with a year-long cache; the page asks for it with ?v=, so a new drawing is a
   new URL. Plain text, no script: the page shows it as an image.
     fireflies.svg        Uranium mode's hero: glowing mushrooms in a night wood, fireflies drifting (from the owner,
                          2026-10-10), exactly worker/art/prowl-hero-fireflies.svg. Animated (SMIL), for screens with a
                          mouse: on a phone it kept a mid-range main thread a third to a half busy.
     fireflies-still.svg  the same drawing at its first frame, for phones (hover:none): every animation taken out, each
                          firefly where it starts and as bright, the glow as it begins.
     glowworms.svg        Cockpit mode's hero (worker v177, Matt: "a red mushroom animation or ... a glowing worm"): a
                          cave roof hung with glowworm threads whose beads pulse red, glowing red mushrooms on the floor,
                          sparks drifting up. Exactly worker/art/prowl-hero-glowworms.svg; drawn in the same SMIL forms
                          as the fireflies, so stillSvg makes its phone frame.
     glowworms-still.svg  its first frame.
     bloodmoon.webp       Cockpit mode's hero since v197 (Matt, 2026-10-31: "fix the mushroom and panther illustration, make
                          it look more professional", then his blood moon photo): a red moon rising behind a forest, a
                          mossy floor for the panther to stand on. 1600 px wide, for screens over 480 px.
     bloodmoon-sm.webp    the same photo 800 px wide, for phones.
   The photos are worker/art/prowl-hero-bloodmoon*.webp, carried as base64 in art-photos.js (scripts/build-hero-photos.mjs). */
